window.docContents[208].resolve({"/Taking-Terms-Apart/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Taking-Terms-Apart--The-View-of-the-Imported-Theories":{"contents":"Each theory comes with a view of its operators, and def.term_view V gathers the views of every theory the current module imports into one inductive V. A theory that is not imported is not viewed: its terms fall into V's catch-all, other. Besides one constructor per operator, V has leaves for values, declared symbols and bound variables.\n\nsection\nvariable [Ω]\nopen Typed\ndef.term_view V\nend\n\n\nIn the typed layer V : Typ → Type: V τ is a term of sort τ taken apart. Each operator has a constructor whose kids are typed at their sorts — a comparison's operand sort is a field, which types its kids:\n\n#check @V.lt\n\n\n@V.lt : [inst : Ω] → (α : Typ) → {h0 : α.isArith = true} → Typed.Kids α.Denote → V Typ.bool\n\n\nV.of τ t views a term t of sort τ. Matching on the sort alongside the view refines both: at .lt .int ks, the kids ks are Term Ints.\n\nopen Typed in #eval Env.runIO do\n  let x ← Term.mkSymbolAs Int \"x\"\n  let t ← smt! x + 1 < 2 * x\n  match ← V.of .bool t with\n  | .lt .int ks =>\n    let kids : Array (Term Int) := ks.val\n    println! \"an integer comparison of {kids}\"\n  | _ => println! \"something else\"\n\n\nan integer comparison of #[(+ x 1), (* 2 x)]\n\n\nMatching at the wrong sort is caught statically: the kids of a real comparison are not integers.\n\nopen Typed in\nexample [Ω] (v : V .bool) : Option (Kids Int) :=\n  match v with\n  | .lt .real ks => some ks\n  | _ => none\n\n\nApplication type mismatch: The argument\n  ks\nhas type\n  Kids Rat\nbut is expected to have type\n  Kids Int\nin the application\n  some ks\n\nNote: The following definitions were not unfolded because their definition is not exposed:\n  Term ↦ 4\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level API for CVC5\u0009Taking Terms Apart","header":"5.1. The View of the Imported Theories","id":"/Taking-Terms-Apart/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Taking-Terms-Apart--The-View-of-the-Imported-Theories"}});